WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.568
The school asks for more than separate definitions. You must move through an encounter, showing how each observation changes the next decision. This session connects the Week One teaching into two original simulation variants.
学校要求不只是分开的定义，而是走完整个接触过程，展示每个观察怎样改变下一决定。本节用两个原创模拟变式串联第一周教学。

00:00:14.568 --> 00:00:29.448
The first variant practises the approach to a prone unresponsive person. The second combines a fall with an underlying illness and hidden deterioration. They rehearse school task types without reproducing a school assessment answer.
第一个变式练习接近俯卧无反应者；第二个把跌倒、基础疾病及隐匿恶化相连。它们练习学校任务类型，不复制学校考核答案。

00:00:29.448 --> 00:00:43.104
Use a trainer and an observer for physical tasks. The observer gives only information actually available at each stage; the team must request or obtain the rest instead of assuming a normal examination.
操作任务使用模拟器及观察者。观察者只给当前确实可获得的资料，团队必须询问或检查其余内容，不能假定正常。

00:00:43.104 --> 00:00:55.704
The goal is a complete reasoning and action chain, not speed without care. The school timed rotation is a practice structure, not a guarantee of competence or permission for unsupervised treatment.
目标是完整推理行动链，而非只求快。学校限时轮转是练习结构，不是能力保证，也不授权无督导治疗。

00:00:55.704 --> 00:01:06.792
At the start, identify a lead and assign the immediate work. A task such as check breathing and tell me rate, depth and adequacy is clearer than somebody do vitals.
开始时明确带领者及即时分工。“查呼吸并报告频率、深度及是否足够”比“谁去量体征”清楚。

00:01:06.792 --> 00:01:18.384
Use closed-loop communication: a named person acknowledges, performs and reports the result. The lead confirms that the result has been heard and changes the plan when necessary.
闭环沟通是点名人员确认、执行并报告结果，带领者确认听见，并在必要时改变计划。

00:01:18.384 --> 00:01:30.048
Roles can change as the patient changes. If two providers are needed for effective ventilation, stop nonessential recording or equipment tidying and redirect the available hands.
患者变化时角色可改变。有效通气若需两人，应暂停非必要记录或整理，重新配置人手。

00:01:30.048 --> 00:01:42.552
The recorder documents what actually happened, including delay or uncertainty. A neat record assembled from guessed values is less useful than an honest chronology of a difficult simulation.
记录员写实际发生内容，包括延误及不确定。靠猜值拼出的整洁记录，不如困难模拟中真实时序有用。

00:01:42.552 --> 00:01:54.072
In this original variant, an adult is found face down beside a bicycle path. Control the moving-traffic risk and preserve access before committing the team beside the person.
本原创变式中，一名成人俯卧在自行车道旁。到患者身旁前，先控制流动交通风险并保留通道。

00:01:54.072 --> 00:02:07.416
Ask bystanders what they directly saw, when the person was last known responsive and whether a collision or collapse preceded the position. Attribute those reports rather than converting them into confirmed findings.
问旁观者直接看见什么、最后何时有反应，以及是否先碰撞或倒下。应标明报告来源，不把它们变成已证实发现。

00:02:07.416 --> 00:02:20.736
Check responsiveness and obvious immediately accessible threats while planning access to the airway and chest. A rigid recital of a scene checklist must not obscure an urgent functional problem.
计划接近气道胸部时，检查反应及立即能见的威胁。不能僵硬背现场清单，忽视紧急功能问题。

00:02:20.736 --> 00:02:32.976
Unknown cause keeps both injury and illness in view. Spinal concern changes handling, but does not justify leaving an inaccessible, threatened airway unassessed indefinitely.
原因不明时，受伤和疾病都要保留。脊柱顾虑改变搬动方式，但不能据此无限期不检查无法接近的濒危气道。

00:02:32.976 --> 00:02:45.696
The selected Nancy airway page directs a prone unresponsive patient to be positioned for airway and breathing assessment, using a unit log roll. It does not make a blocked airway safer to leave face down.
所选 Nancy 气道页要求将俯卧无反应者以整体翻转重新摆位，以便检查气道呼吸。气道受阻者并不会因一直面朝下而更安全。

00:02:45.696 --> 00:03:00.792
Plan with the actual team and trainer. State who coordinates, who controls the relevant body regions and where the patient will end up. Prepare suction and ventilation equipment before a move likely to reveal an airway problem.
根据实际团队及模拟器规划，说明谁协调、谁控制各身体区域、最终放哪。若搬动可能暴露气道问题，应先备好吸引及通气设备。

00:03:00.792 --> 00:03:13.704
The principle is coordinated movement as a unit, with spinal motion minimized when indicated. Do not twist the head independently of the trunk or force an injured body into a position against resistance.
原则是整体协调移动，需要时尽量减少脊柱活动。不要头部独立于躯干扭转，也不要克服阻力强迫受伤身体摆位。

00:03:13.704 --> 00:03:25.608
Your instructor must demonstrate the actual personnel arrangement and approved technique. Practise with a suitable manikin rather than an unsupported improvised roll on a real person.
具体人员位置及获准技术由教员示范。应在适当模拟人上练习，不在真人身上做缺乏支持的临时翻转。

00:03:25.608 --> 00:03:36.480
Repositioning is not the endpoint. Immediately inspect and open or clear the airway as needed, assess actual breathing and circulation, and act on the findings.
重新摆位不是终点。应立即检查、按需开放清理气道，评估实际呼吸循环，并据发现行动。

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:51.504
A patient who is not breathing normally needs the appropriate resuscitation branch. A patient who is breathing adequately but cannot protect the airway needs protection and close monitoring under the actual injury and positioning context.
无正常呼吸者需走适当复苏分支；呼吸足够但无法保护气道者，则须按实际伤情及体位背景保护并密切监测。

00:03:51.504 --> 00:04:02.976
Do not call the roll successful just because the person is supine. Check whether the airway became obstructed, support detached, bleeding changed or an injury became more apparent.
不能仅因已仰卧就叫翻身成功。应查气道是否阻塞、支持是否脱落、出血是否改变或损伤是否更明显。

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:14.448
State the result aloud and record the major move and subsequent reassessment. This makes the handoff more useful and gives the observer evidence of a safe action-response loop.
应口述结果，记录重大搬动及随后复评，让交接更有用，也让观察者看见安全行动反应循环。

00:04:14.448 --> 00:04:29.400
Name and perform the school primary-survey tasks, but treat the immediate life threat when found. Current A two explicitly prioritizes catastrophic bleeding and coordinates unconscious breathing and circulation assessment.
应说出并执行学校初评任务，但发现即时生命威胁就处理。现行 A02 明确优先致命出血，并协调无意识者呼吸及循环评估。

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:41.400
Rapid body survey looks for important concealed threats without turning the first minutes into a routine complete examination. Explain exposure, maintain warmth and protect dignity.
快速全身扫查寻找重要隐匿威胁，不把最初几分钟变成例行完整检查。应解释暴露、保暖并维护尊严。

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:55.512
SOAPPP is the school stabilization reminder; the saved BCPEG intervention wording is different. In either source, select indicated care, not automatic oxygen or an adjunct for every patient.
SOAPPP 是学校稳定化提示；现存 BCPEG 干预措辞不同。无论采用哪一来源，都应选有适应证照护，而非人人自动上氧或辅助气道。

00:04:55.512 --> 00:05:09.120
The useful verbalization is finding, meaning, action and reassessment. Saying airway clear while never examining it, or calling breathing adequate from a saturation alone, does not show the skill.
有用口述是发现、意义、行动及复评。没检查就说气道通畅，或只凭血氧说呼吸足够，不能展示技能。

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:23.112
After identifying and addressing immediate threats, state your transport category and the findings supporting it. The BCPEG generic flow permits earlier conveyance when condition and definitive-care needs require it.
识别处理即时威胁后，说明转运类别及支持发现。BCPEG 通用流程允许按病情及确定性治疗需要更早转运。

00:05:23.112 --> 00:05:34.632
Distinguish an action that changes immediate survival from a routine task that can occur en route. A school scene-time benchmark is not permission to use every remaining minute before leaving.
应区分立即影响生存的行动，与可途中进行的例行任务。学校现场时间基准，不是允许用完剩余每一分钟才离开。

00:05:34.632 --> 00:05:47.712
Movement needs an equipment and staffing plan, especially if airway support must continue. Check the route, straps, device security and access to the patient before committing to a narrow space.
搬动需设备及人员计划，尤其气道支持要持续时。进入狭窄空间前，核查路线、固定带、器械及能否接近患者。

00:05:47.712 --> 00:06:03.168
Use an early report to request appropriate resources and prepare the receiver. Exact destination and clinical pathway depend on the actual presentation and service system; urgency does not justify an invented local rule.
及早报告以获取适当资源、让接收方准备。具体目的地及路径依实际表现和系统决定，紧急不等于可以编造当地规则。

00:06:03.168 --> 00:06:14.688
The second original simulation uses a seventy-seven-year-old man with hip pain after a fall. Family report that he is normally independent but is unusually confused today.
第二个原创模拟为七十七岁男性跌倒后髋痛。家属说平时独立，今天却异常混乱。

00:06:14.688 --> 00:06:27.720
Do not close the case as a simple mechanical fall. Ask whether illness, faintness or another problem caused the event, and examine both the possible injury and the current physiological disturbance.
不能草率归为简单机械性跌倒。询问是否先有疾病、晕厥感或其他问题，既检查可能伤情，也检查当前生理紊乱。

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:43.152
Anticoagulant use and uncertain head impact are important reported risks, not proof of a brain bleed. Attribute the history, seek missing details and communicate uncertainty rather than making a false definitive diagnosis.
服抗凝药及不确定撞头是重要病史风险，不证明颅内出血。应标来源、补缺项并沟通不确定，而非虚假确诊。

00:06:43.152 --> 00:06:57.672
New confusion changes urgency independently of the pain complaint. Establish the previous baseline and timeline, check glucose and complete the immediate functional assessment before an extended orthopedic history.
新发混乱独立于疼痛改变紧迫性。应明确既往基线及时序、查血糖，在长篇骨科病史前完成即时功能评估。

00:06:57.672 --> 00:07:10.368
Ask a question because its answer can change the plan. Medication history should establish actual names, use, timing and relevant doses, not simply that the patient takes pills.
提问应因为答案能改变计划。用药史须明确实际名称、使用、时间及相关剂量，而非只知道“吃药”。

00:07:10.368 --> 00:07:26.424
For pain, obtain location, radiation, quality, onset and provoking factors, plus a patient-reported severity and trend. Do not deliberately repeat painful movement to reproduce a finding that is already clear.
疼痛需查部位、放射、性质、起始、诱发因素，及患者自报程度和趋势。已明确发现不需为重现而故意反复做痛性动作。

00:07:26.424 --> 00:07:39.336
For the fall, establish the mechanism, possible loss of consciousness and subsequent movement. Ask what happened before the fall; an illness causing collapse may be the more time-critical problem.
跌倒需明确机制、可能意识丧失及随后搬动；还要问跌倒之前发生什么，致晕倒疾病可能更紧迫。

00:07:39.336 --> 00:07:54.240
Include functional inquiry: what could the person do yesterday and what can they do now? If confusion limits reliability, document collateral information and unresolved questions rather than forcing a complete-sounding history.
应含功能询问：昨天能做什么、现在能做什么？混乱影响可靠性时，应记录旁证及未答问题，不强凑听起来完整的病史。

00:07:54.240 --> 00:08:07.200
The observer now provides measured values, not a diagnosis: twenty-six breaths, saturation ninety-five on air, pulse one hundred twelve and manual pressure one hundred two over sixty-four.
观察者现在提供实测值，不给诊断：呼吸二十六次、空气中血氧九十五、脉一百一十二，手测血压一百零二比六十四。

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:22.080
Temperature is thirty-eight point four by the stated method, and glucose is six point eight millimoles per litre. New confusion was established against the reported baseline, not inferred from an unfamiliar accent or hearing problem.
按所述方法体温三十八点四，血糖每升六点八毫摩尔。新混乱依据既往基线确认，不从陌生口音或听力问题推断。

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:34.320
Verify measurement quality and record time, method and oxygen context. If a number conflicts with the examination, recheck it without delaying support for an obvious clinical threat.
核实测量质量，记录时刻、方法及给氧背景。数字与检查不符时应复测，但不因此延误明显临床威胁的支持。

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:46.680
A single glucose within a usual range does not make the patient stable. The complete pattern and trajectory determine concern, while each exact number allows another clinician to check your reasoning.
一个处于通常范围的血糖，不会让患者变稳定。担忧依据完整模式及趋势，而精确数字可让他人复核推理。

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:57.384
For this adult example, use scale one. Twenty-six breaths scores three and ninety-five percent scores one. On air there are no added oxygen points.
本成人例用量表一。每分钟二十六次计三分，百分之九十五计一分；空气中无补氧附加分。

00:08:57.384 --> 00:09:08.040
A systolic pressure of one hundred two scores one, pulse one hundred twelve scores two, temperature thirty-eight point four scores one and new confusion scores three.
收缩压一百零二计一分，脉一百一十二计两分，体温三十八点四计一分，新混乱计三分。

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:21.024
Add all six contributions to obtain eleven. Do not leave consciousness out because a GCS is also charted, or forget oxygen points if you later calculate a new score during supplemental oxygen.
六项相加得十一分。不能因另记 GCS 就漏意识；之后若在吸氧下重新评分，也不能漏补氧分。

00:09:21.024 --> 00:09:34.680
This high aggregate and single severe parameter support urgent escalation, but do not diagnose the cause. You still need the clinical examination, repeated observations and the applicable ambulance pathway.
高总分及单项严重异常支持紧急升级，但不能诊断病因。仍需临床检查、连续观察及适用救护路径。

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:50.688
Fever, confusion, tachypnea and circulation changes raise concern for infection-associated deterioration, including possible sepsis. A temperature alone cannot establish it, and absence of fever would not safely exclude it.
发热、混乱、呼吸快及循环变化提示感染相关恶化，包括可能脓毒症。单凭体温不能确诊，无发热也不能安全排除。

00:09:50.688 --> 00:10:03.888
The fall also raises injury concerns, and anticoagulation increases the importance of an accurate history and examination. Infection and injury are not mutually exclusive explanations.
跌倒还带来伤情担忧，抗凝使准确病史及检查更重要。感染与受伤不是互斥解释。

00:10:03.888 --> 00:10:16.944
Do not explain every abnormality as pain or assume that one plausible diagnosis accounts for all findings. State the urgent physiological problem and preserve the serious alternatives in the report.
不能把所有异常都归疼痛，也不能假定一个合理诊断解释全部。应指出紧急生理问题，并在报告保留重要备选。

00:10:16.944 --> 00:10:29.976
Provide indicated support, escalate and reassess. Do not make an unstable patient walk merely to test the hip, and do not administer a treatment simply because a score has a particular value.
给予有适应证支持、升级并复评。不能只为测试髋部让不稳定者走，也不能只因评分某数值就给某治疗。

00:10:29.976 --> 00:10:43.632
Explain the movement and obtain the applicable cooperation or authority. Choose the approved method according to suspected injury, patient size, tolerance, staffing and route rather than convenience alone.
解释搬动，取得适用配合或权限。按疑伤、体型、耐受、人员及路线选获准方法，而非只图方便。

00:10:43.632 --> 00:10:56.616
Coordinate the movement under one lead and minimize unnecessary painful motion. Maintain access to any support and protect lines, oxygen tubing and monitoring leads from entanglement.
由一人带领协调，减少无必要痛性活动。保持支持可接近，防止管路、氧管及监护线缠绕。

00:10:56.616 --> 00:11:08.736
After the major move, repeat the relevant assessment rather than copying the earlier numbers. If the patient worsens, stop where safe, reassess and address the immediate problem.
重大搬动后重做相关评估，不复制早先数字。患者恶化时，在安全处停下，复评并处理即时问题。

00:11:08.736 --> 00:11:21.288
Document the movement method, assistance and response. A patient who was stable on the floor can deteriorate during packaging, so the reassessment is a clinical action, not a documentation formality.
记录搬动方法、协助及反应。地上暂稳者可在包装中恶化，所以复评是临床行动，不是记录形式。

00:11:21.288 --> 00:11:34.512
Begin with your role and the urgent concern: an older fall patient has new confusion and abnormal physiology. Do not open with an extended chronological story that hides the reason for calling.
以角色及紧急担忧开头：老年跌倒者有新混乱和异常生理。不要长篇按时间讲故事，把呼叫原因埋住。

00:11:34.512 --> 00:11:48.288
Give the relevant baseline and history, then exact observations with time and oxygen context. State NEWS2 eleven and the components that matter; the number should summarize evidence, not replace it.
给相关基线及病史，再报带时刻和供氧背景的精确观察。报 NEWS2 十一及重要分项，数字概括证据，不替代证据。

00:11:48.288 --> 00:12:01.512
Report what was actually done and the response, then make the request explicit. If a treatment or examination has not yet occurred, say so rather than speaking in a way that implies completion.
报告实际做过什么及反应，再明确请求。治疗或检查尚未发生就直说，不用暗示已经完成的措辞。

00:12:01.512 --> 00:12:15.048
Confirm instructions with a read-back when appropriate and document them. A consultation does not transfer patient responsibility by itself; the later transfer uses the applicable handover structure and acceptance.
适当时回读确认指示并记录。咨询本身不等于转移患者责任，之后交接采用适用结构并确认接收。

00:12:15.048 --> 00:12:29.712
A timeline distinguishes event time from charting time. In this fictional demonstration, contact is ten hundred and the measured baseline is ten hundred four; do not backdate a later observation to the initial encounter.
时序区分事件时刻与书写时刻。本虚构示范接触为十点，测量基线为十点零四；不能把后来观察倒填成刚接触。

00:12:29.712 --> 00:12:45.528
Each action needs its reason and response. If oxygen is given, document the indication, device, flow and effect. If a task is declined or not possible, record what, why and what alternative was used.
每个行动要有理由和反应。给氧则记适应证、器械、流量及效果。拒绝或无法完成的任务，要记什么、为什么及替代做法。

00:12:45.528 --> 00:12:58.320
Do not invent the second observation set to finish a worksheet. The simulator or actual examination must provide the value; a blank or explained omission is more truthful than a copied baseline.
不能为填完表而编第二套观察。数值须来自模拟提供或实际检查；空白或解释遗漏，比复制基线真实。

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:10.296
Keep case information separate from real patient data. The demonstration is for learning the record structure; the student produces the actual school practice PCR from their own observed station.
案例资料与真实患者资料分开。示范用来学记录结构；实际学校练习 PCR 由学生根据本人观察站点自写。

00:13:10.296 --> 00:13:24.600
The local BCPEG page seventeen is an image of the blank examination PCR. Its history boxes and examination fields are separate, so attribute reported information and keep it distinct from findings you obtained.
当地 BCPEG 第十七页是空白考试 PCR 图像。病史格与检查栏分开，因此报告资料要标来源，并区别于本人所得发现。

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:39.264
Its serial table includes GCS components and vital observations. Enter actual units and methods where needed, and record a non-testable component or an unobtainable measurement honestly rather than inventing a normal.
连续表含 GCS 分项及生命观察。按需记单位方法；分项无法测试或测量无法取得，应如实记录，不能编正常值。

00:13:39.264 --> 00:13:52.704
Use the care, protocol and additional-comment areas to connect actions, reasons and response. A tick beside oxygen does not replace its relevant device, flow and effect information.
用照护、流程及补充评论区连接行动、理由及反应。氧气旁打勾，不替代相关器械、流量及效果资料。

00:13:52.704 --> 00:14:08.424
Check identifiers, chronology, internal consistency and handover details before finalizing. Corrections must preserve the original record according to the actual documentation system; never erase an inconvenient observation.
完成前核查身份、时序、内部一致及交接细节。更正按实际系统保留原记录，不能擦掉不方便的观察。

00:14:08.424 --> 00:14:19.896
Explain why each protective item is needed for the task and anticipated exposure. Equipment selection and correct removal matter more than wearing the greatest possible number of items.
解释每件防护为何对应任务及预期暴露。选择恰当并正确脱除，比穿最多件更重要。

00:14:19.896 --> 00:14:35.160
Use the taught current procedure, including the respirator fit and seal requirements when relevant. The paired reading identifies the archived checklist separately so its sequence is not silently treated as every current local procedure.
使用当前所教规程，相关时含呼吸防护器适合性及密合要求。对照阅读另标存档清单，不把它默认为所有现行当地规程。

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:47.688
Ask the observer to identify a contamination event such as a dirty glove touching a clean meter. Stop, clean or replace the affected items as required and repair the clean-dirty workflow.
让观察者指出污染事件，例如脏手套碰洁净血糖仪。应停下，按需清洁或更换受影响物，并修复脏净流程。

00:14:47.688 --> 00:14:59.832
Report an exposure promptly under the applicable procedure. A perfect-looking final glove removal does not undo contamination that already travelled to equipment, clothing or mucosa.
暴露应按规程及时报告。最后手套脱得再漂亮，也不能消除此前传到设备、衣物或黏膜的污染。

00:14:59.832 --> 00:15:13.752
The school introduces a thirty-minute PAA rotation. Unless the instructor supplies a more specific station schedule, use that as the overall practice container rather than inventing mandatory minute-by-minute scoring rules.
学校引入三十分钟 PAA 轮转。教员未另给站点时程时，把它作为整体练习时段，不编造强制逐分钟评分规则。

00:15:13.752 --> 00:15:23.976
Complete the case, report and a brief record outline, then debrief the decisive branch: what did you notice, what did it mean, what did you do and what changed?
完成案例、报告及简短记录提纲，再复盘决定性分支：注意了什么、意味着什么、做了什么、随后变了什么？

00:15:23.976 --> 00:15:37.008
Have each member lead and observe across repeated rotations. Change a meaningful feature rather than memorizing one script, such as normal versus ineffective breathing or a stable versus falling pressure.
重复轮转让每人都带领及观察。改变有意义特征，例如正常与无效呼吸、稳定与下降血压，不要只背一份脚本。

00:15:37.008 --> 00:15:50.184
Choose a specific improvement to test immediately: a clearer task instruction, better cuff positioning or an earlier airway reassessment. Feedback should name observed behaviour rather than judge the person.
选具体改进马上再试：更清晰分工、袖带摆位更好或更早重查气道。反馈应指出观察行为，而非评判人格。

00:15:50.184 --> 00:16:07.680
The school links a short BVM demonstration in its Weekend One practical resources. First identify the clinical branch: a ventilation problem is not the same as isolated low oxygen saturation, and the current trained resuscitation pathway determines the sequence.
学校在第一周实训资源中链接了 BVM 示范视频。先确定临床分支：通气问题不等同于单纯血氧偏低，具体顺序由当前训练的复苏路径决定。

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:20.088
BVM provides positive-pressure breaths when spontaneous ventilation is absent or inadequate. It cannot compensate for an obstructed upper airway until the passage is opened or cleared.
自主通气停止或不足时，BVM 可提供正压呼吸；但上气道被阻塞时，必须先开放或清理通道，球囊不能绕过阻塞。

00:16:20.088 --> 00:16:34.080
Airway patency, oxygenation and ventilation are related but distinct. A reassuring saturation does not prove adequate ventilation, and oxygen through a mask alone does not replace a missing breath.
气道通畅、氧合和通气相互关联但并不相同。血氧看似正常不能证明通气充分，面罩给氧也不能代替缺失的呼吸。

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:50.904
Do not memorize one ventilation rate for every situation. A pulse-present respiratory-arrest branch, cardiac arrest and a procedure-specific PEEP technique may have different instructions; identify the patient and use the current school/service protocol.
不要背一个频率套用所有情况。有脉搏呼吸骤停、心搏骤停及特定 PEEP 操作可能采用不同指示；先识别患者，再按学校/机构现行规程执行。

00:16:50.904 --> 00:17:07.944
Use the school video to recognize the equipment and see one demonstration, not as a substitute for checking the device in your own lab. The assembly, oxygen reservoir and connections vary by model; follow that manufacturer’s instructions and the instructor’s checkoff.
通过学校视频熟悉器材并观看一种示范，但不能代替在实训室检查实际器械。不同型号的组装、氧气储气袋和连接不同；应遵守制造商说明及教师核查表。

00:17:07.944 --> 00:17:24.312
Before use, inspect that the mask suits the patient, the bag and one-way valve function, the oxygen source is connected when indicated, and tubing and reservoir are arranged for the actual model. A familiar-looking bag is not proof that it works.
使用前检查面罩适合患者、球囊和单向阀正常；按需要连接氧源，并按实际型号连接管路及储气袋。外观看起来熟悉，不证明器械有效。

00:17:24.312 --> 00:17:37.128
Position yourself where the airway and chest can be seen. In a team, name who maintains the airway and mask seal, who delivers breaths, and who watches chest movement and reports changes.
站在能观察气道和胸部的位置。团队中明确谁维持气道及面罩密封、谁送气、谁观察胸廓运动并报告变化。

00:17:37.128 --> 00:17:50.016
If secretions or vomit threaten patency, have appropriate suction ready and use the taught technique. Protect against exposure using current routine practices and task-specific precautions.
分泌物或呕吐物可能影响通畅时，备好适当吸引并按所教方法操作。按现行常规防护及任务风险采取暴露防护。

00:17:50.016 --> 00:18:10.296
BCEHS B01 identifies a patent airway and a tight mask seal as prerequisites for effective BVM. With loss of airway tone, the jaw thrust is an effective opening maneuver; where cervical injury is not suspected, the current guideline describes jaw thrust and head-tilt/chin-lift together.
BCEHS B01 指出，气道通畅及面罩密封是有效 BVM 的前提。气道肌张力丧失时，下颌前移是有效开放手法；不怀疑颈椎损伤时，现行指南描述下颌前移与仰头抬颏合用。

00:18:10.296 --> 00:18:22.608
BCEHS says optimal BVM ventilation is performed by two providers. One can maintain jaw position and the mask seal while the other delivers breaths and watches the patient with the team.
BCEHS 指出最佳 BVM 通气由两名操作者完成。一人维持下颌位置及面罩密封，另一人送气并与团队一起观察患者。

00:18:22.608 --> 00:18:38.712
The school’s linked video is an older visual resource. A sampled frame explains the E-C hand technique when an EMT is alone; that is a useful contrast, not evidence that a lone-rescuer grip is preferable when a second provider is available.
学校链接的视频是较早的视觉资源。抽查画面解释了急救人员独自操作时的 E-C 手法；这可用来比较，但不能证明有第二名操作者时单人握法更优。

00:18:38.712 --> 00:18:51.144
Practice the hand placement on the school’s manikin using the instructor’s chosen method. Never infer that a correctly shaped grip guarantees an open airway, a seal or a delivered breath.
应按教师选定的方法在学校模拟人上练习手位。不能以手型正确就推断气道开放、密封良好或呼吸已送达。

00:18:51.144 --> 00:19:06.696
BCEHS B01 calls for the chest to be appropriately exposed so that ventilation effectiveness is judged by chest rise. Only a slight but definite rise is needed for safe ventilation; more bag compression is not automatically better.
BCEHS B01 要求适当暴露胸部，以胸廓抬起判断通气是否有效。安全通气只需轻微但明确的抬起；球囊挤得更多并不自动更好。

00:19:06.696 --> 00:19:19.800
If the chest does not rise, stop and troubleshoot rather than forcing larger breaths: recheck airway position, mask fit, obstruction, equipment and the need for trained help or an adjunct.
胸廓未抬起时，应停下排查，而不是强行加大呼吸量：重查气道位置、面罩贴合、阻塞、器械，以及是否需要受训支援或辅助器。

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:32.544
Watch the patient’s work of breathing, color, responsiveness and perfusion, and compare with the pre-support state. A pulse-oximeter value may lag and does not measure ventilation directly.
观察患者呼吸功、肤色、反应及灌注，并与支持前状态比较。脉搏血氧数值可能滞后，也不直接测量通气。

00:19:32.544 --> 00:19:47.616
Capnography can add useful ventilation information when available and appropriate, but it does not replace visible patient assessment or the actual local pathway. If the patient worsens, escalate and reassess immediately.
条件适当且可用时，二氧化碳波形可补充通气信息，但不能代替患者直接评估或当地实际流程。患者恶化时应立即升级处置并复评。

00:19:47.616 --> 00:20:01.704
The school-link viewer did not provide an exportable transcript during review, so this lesson does not claim a complete spoken-content summary. Use the clip for visual orientation and follow the captions available in your own course player.
核对时学校链接视频没有可导出的文字稿，因此本课不声称已完整总结其口述内容。请把视频用于视觉熟悉，并按你课程播放器中实际提供的字幕学习。

00:20:01.704 --> 00:20:15.720
Pause the video to identify what the operator’s hands are doing, whether the airway remains positioned, what feedback the chest gives and whether another helper is present. Do not copy a movement without understanding its purpose.
可暂停视频，辨认操作者手部动作、气道是否保持体位、胸部反馈如何，以及是否有另一位助手。不要不理解目的就照搬动作。

00:20:15.720 --> 00:20:29.376
Then practise with the actual school equipment and manikin. The observer should report visible chest rise, seal problems and changes in the patient scenario; give one specific correction and repeat the attempt.
之后用学校实际器材和模拟人练习。观察者报告可见胸廓起伏、密封问题及患者情境变化；给出一项具体纠正后再练一次。

00:20:29.376 --> 00:20:42.648
Watching or playing a video is not proof of physical competence. The instructor’s current technique, relevant authorization, device instructions and supervised checkoff remain the standard for performance.
观看或播放视频不能证明已掌握实操。实际操作仍以教师当前技术、相关授权、器械说明及督导技能核验为准。

00:20:42.648 --> 00:20:56.928
Before the school check, explain why your priority changed in each case, calculate a new NEWS2 and identify what the number cannot diagnose. This tests understanding rather than recognition of familiar words.
学校检查前，应解释案例中优先为何改变、计算新的 NEWS2，并指出数字不能诊断什么。这测理解，不只认熟词。

00:20:56.928 --> 00:21:09.744
Demonstrate the applicable skills under supervision: PPE, measurement, safe coordinated repositioning and the PAA encounter. Playback completion does not replace the instructor observation.
在督导下展示适用技能：PPE、测量、安全协调摆位及 PAA 接触。播放完成不替代教员观察。

00:21:09.744 --> 00:21:23.472
The school pre-quiz requirement remains a student task; the saved outline states at least seventy-five percent. This course neither opens the quiz nor supplies its answers or a fabricated completion.
学校课前测要求仍由学生完成；现存提纲写至少百分之七十五。本课程不打开测验，不提供答案或虚构完成。

00:21:23.472 --> 00:21:37.008
Use the reading tracker to distinguish taught concepts from unresolved assigned-edition coverage. The next week builds on these functions, so repair a specific weak decision or technique instead of just collecting more notes.
用阅读跟踪区分已教概念与未解指定版本范围。下一周以这些功能为基础，应修复具体薄弱决策或技术，而非只收更多笔记。
